<.shell title="Overview" current={:index}>
  <h1>Style guide</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A design system for operational tools: search and rescue, emergency services, and teams
    like them. GOV.UK's patterns and plain look, Carbon's dense tables, in light and dark.
  </p>

  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Plain and calm.</strong>
      People use this between calls and after long days. Short words, one primary action per page,
      nothing that moves without a reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dense where people scan, roomy where they type.</strong>
      Tables use 32px rows, or 24px when compact. Forms keep 40px inputs and big targets.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Desktop first, phone second.</strong>
      Pages are designed for a laptop. On a phone everything still works and nothing breaks:
      layouts stack, and tables scroll sideways with the useful columns first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Keyboard first.</strong>
      Everything you can reach shows the yellow focus, the same in both modes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fixed scales.</strong>
      Six type sizes, eight spaces, and a named palette. No value is invented on a page; if a
      design needs a new one, it joins the scale.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tokens, then modes.</strong>
      Components use colour tokens only, so dark mode is a second set of values, not a second
      set of styles.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the examples are made</h2>
  <p>
    Every example is drawn by the app's own components and stylesheet, so it looks as it does
    in the app. A few show a design no page uses yet, and say so.
  </p>

  <h2>Pages</h2>
  <.table
    id="guide-pages"
    rows={[
      {:colors, "Colours", "Every token in light and dark, and what each is for."},
      {:typography, "Typography", "The type scale, headings, body text, numbers, and links."},
      {:writing, "Writing",
       "The rules and glossary for every word a person reads. Agents follow it."},
      {:icons, "Icons", "The small set of icons, their sizes, and when to use one."},
      {:layout, "Layout", "Spacing, page headers, detail lists, cards, and stats."},
      {:components, "Buttons and tags", "Button kinds and sizes, tags, and focus."},
      {:navigation, "Navigation", "The top bar, breadcrumbs, tabs, and pagination."},
      {:feedback, "Messages", "Toasts, banners, warnings, errors, empty states, and loading."},
      {:tables, "Tables", "Dense and compact tables, from the app's real pages."},
      {:forms, "Forms", "Every input, errors, and the app's real forms."},
      {:charts, "Charts and maps",
       "Stats, columns, lines, heat grids, bar lists, and the activity map."}
    ]}
  >
    <:col :let={{page, title, _about}} label="Page" class="w-px whitespace-nowrap">
      <.a href={page_path(page)}>{title}</.a>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_page, _title, about}} label="What it covers">{about}</:col>
  </.table>
</.shell>
